  "Question": "If \\(f(x)=ax^4-bx^2+x+5\\) and \\(f(-3)=2,\\) then \\(f(3)=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-5\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "We do not need to find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) separately. The even powers have the same values at \\(3\\) and \\(-3\\), so subtracting the two function values eliminates both unknown coefficients:\n\\[\nf(3)=81a-9b+8,\n\\]\n\\[\nf(-3)=81a-9b+2.\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\nf(3)-f(-3)=6.\n\\]\nSince \\(f(-3)=2\\), we obtain \\(f(3)=2+6=\\boxed{8}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
